    "preview": "# Enterprise Data Governance Knowledge Guide for Database: codebase_community\n\n## 1. Introduction\nThis Knowledge Guide serves as a comprehensive semantic layer for the database \"codebase_community,\" providing authoritative guidance on data governance standards, core business entities, metric definitions, constraints, and exemplar use cases. It is designed to ensure consistency, accuracy, and clarity in data interpretation and usage across the enterprise.\n\n## 2. Core Entities & Fields\n\n### Users\n- **Id**: Unique identifier for each user.\n- **Display Name**: The name displayed publicly for the user.\n- **Reputation**: Numerical value representing the user's standing within the community.\n- **Creation Date**: Date when the user account was created.\n- **Last Access Date**: Date of the user's most recent access.\n- **Location**: Geographical location of the user.\n- **Age**: Age of the user.\n- **Views**: Number of times the user's profile has been viewed.\n- **UpVotes/DownVotes**: Count of upvotes and downvotes received by the user.\n\n### Posts\n- **Id**: Unique identifier for each post.\n- **Title**: The title of the post.\n- **Body**: The main content of the post.\n- **Score**: Rating score of the post.\n- **View Count**: Number of times the post has been viewed.\n- **Owner User Id**: Identifier for the user who created the post.\n- **Creation Date**: Date when the post was created.\n- **Tags**: Keywords associated with the post.\n- **Answer Count**: Number of answers provided for the post.\n- **Comment Count**: Number of comments on the post.\n- **Favorite Count**: Number of times the post has been marked as a favorite.\n\n### Comments\n- **Id**: Unique identifier for each comment.\n- **Post Id**: Identifier for the post associated with the comment.\n- **Score**: Rating score of the comment.\n- **Text**: Content of the comment.\n- **Creation Date**: Date when the comment was created.\n- **User Id**: Identifier for the user who posted the comment.\n\n### Tags\n- **Id**: Unique identifier for each tag.\n- **Tag Name**: Name of the tag.\n- **Count**: Number of posts associated with the tag.\n- **Excerpt Post Id**: Identifier for the post that provides an excerpt for the tag.\n\n### Votes\n- **Id**: Unique identifier for each vote.\n- **Post Id**: Identifier for the post that received the vote.\n- **Vote Type Id**: Type of vote (e.g., upvote, downvote).\n- **Creation Date**: Date when the vote was cast.\n- **Bounty Amount**: Amount of bounty associated with the vote.\n\n## 3. Metric Definitions\n\n### Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)\n- **User Engagement**: Calculated as the sum of views, upvotes, and downvotes for a user.\n- **Post Popularity**: Determined by the view count and score of a post.\n- **Community Growth**: Measured by the number of new users created within a specific time frame.\n- **Content Quality**: Evaluated by the average score of posts and comments.\n- **Tag Utilization**: Calculated as the count of posts associated with a specific tag.\n\n### Calculation Logic\n- **Average Score**: `AVG(Score)` for posts or comments.\n- **Percentage of Elder Users**: `DIVIDE(COUNT(Id WHERE Age > 65), COUNT(Id)) * 100`.\n- **Post-to-Vote Ratio**: `DIVIDE(Count(post.Id), Count(votes.Id))`.\n\n## 4. Constraints & Conventions\n\n### Filtering Criteria\n- **Temporal Boundaries**: Use `YEAR(CreationDate)` for filtering by year.\n- **Currency Formatting**: Ensure all monetary values are represented in USD.\n- **Unit Conversion**: Age is represented in years; ensure consistency in calculations involving age.\n\n### Common Conventions\n- **Date Format**: Use 'YYYY-MM-DD' for all date-related queries.\n- **Score Thresholds**: Define score thresholds for filtering posts and comments (e.g., Score > 5).\n\n## 5. Exemplar Use Cases\n\n### Example 1: User Reputation Comparison\n**Metric**: Compare the reputation of users \"Harlan\" and \"Jarrod Dixon.\"\n**Explanation**: Identify the user with the highest reputation using `MAX(Reputation)` within the specified display names.\n\n### Example 2: Account Creation Year ",
